Bound and discard the reserved MRS header block without allocating its size.
Related reader hardening: https://github.com/getmikan/Citrus/pull/16

Accept reserved blocks of 0 through 1 MiB and reject invalid lengths before
reading them. Use io.CopyN(io.Discard, ...) instead of allocating a buffer.
The current MRS writer emits an empty reserved block; the binary format and
rule payload are unchanged. This does not impose a decompression memory budget.

Tests cover empty, nonempty and maximum-size blocks for domain and CIDR rules,
truncated blocks, out-of-range lengths and an overflowing length header.

